he product of \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\) is 151200. Now, we need to identify the hundreds digit of this number. The number 151200 can be written as:\n\n\\[ 151200 = 151 \\text{ thousand } 200 \\]\n\nThe hundreds digit is the third digit from the right, which is 2.\n\nThus, the hundreds digit in the product is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
